    "Rc2",
    "Qb4",
    "Rb2"
   ],
   "spoken": "A framework for judging any pin: two factors decide how dangerous it is. First, is the pinned piece shielded by a pawn — if it is, the pin bites far less. Second, how temporary is it — a pin against a king that can castle next move loses almost all its sting. And queens make poor pinners, since they're so easily chased off the job.",
   "kind": "tactic",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 28,
   "t": 952,
   "fen": "r1b2rk1/pp1nqppp/2p1p3/8/2BPP3/2P2N2/PR3PPP/3QK2R w K - 5 15",
   "line": [
    "Qe7"
   ],
   "spoken": "e5 is the thematic strike at the centre, with the pieces perfectly poised — both bearing on that square, so any trade leaves an excellent game. And remember: a mere space advantage is not, by itself, a reason to worry.",
   "kind": "plan",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 994,
   "fen": "r1b2rk1/pp1nqppp/4p3/2p5/2BPP3/2P2N2/PR3PPP/3Q1RK1 w - - 0 16",
